WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.960
There’s been a lot of bombing:&nbsp;
Left right and above, everywhere.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.760
It would be a lie to say I am not&nbsp;
afraid. Because this is a one-way ticket.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.200
I know I’m going there for a good reason.&nbsp;
And if I don’t see my family, my friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.480
and the people I love here on this Earth again,&nbsp;
I have faith that I will meet them after death.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.720
In Ukraine, it’s not just&nbsp;
Ukrainians who are fighting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:49.120
Thousands of people from abroad have joined the&nbsp;
battle. Who are they? Why are they doing it?

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.400
If I’m needed to help my comrades at&nbsp;
the frontline, I’ll go there. If I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.480
needed to take care of civilians, I’ll do that.&nbsp;
Whatever job the legion gives me, I’ll do it.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.760
Kapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.600
as he calls himself, is from Latin America.&nbsp;
For security reasons we don’t disclose his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:26.240
exact location. He is preparing to leave his&nbsp;
home. Kapon tells me he works as a paramedic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:31.840
He seems to have plenty of friends -&nbsp;
overall his life seems pretty normal to me.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.040
He is one of several people I get&nbsp;
in touch with on social media.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.400
Here people who want to join the Ukrainian&nbsp;
army connect from around the globe.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.600
Quite a few men who say they are&nbsp;
already there, post about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.840
But a lot of what they post is hard to verify.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.080
In our first online encounter,&nbsp;
Kapon does not reveal his identity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.840
He wants to join the army as a combat medic.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.960
I saw these terrible images of how they&nbsp;
attacked civilian zones with missiles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.960
people dying in their apartments, and attacks&nbsp;
against humanitarian corridors. I saw so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:26.720
terrible images of suffering civilians, including&nbsp;
children. And it broke my heart to see them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:35.840
And as a paramedic I have the skills to&nbsp;
help them. I know I have something to offer.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.800
The 19-year-old tells me he&nbsp;
still lives with his parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.920
He prefers to not share&nbsp;
pictures of his family though.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.120
They don’t agree with what I’m&nbsp;
doing. The day before yesterday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:57.680
my grandmother was crying. They’re afraid.&nbsp;
And I understand. I’m not going on a holiday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:03.840
I’m going to a country at war and will&nbsp;
risk my life to help other people.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.120
He says his father even offered him money to stay.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.840
But a few days later, it's time to leave.&nbsp;
His friends throw a farewell party.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.520
He sends me videos from his journey: It’s&nbsp;
the first time that he is going abroad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.760
He doesn’t come from a rich&nbsp;
family. The mother of a friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:45.840
chips in to pay for the flight – in return&nbsp;
he has to promise to come back alive.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:56.160
Sandra from Norway has already joined&nbsp;
the Ukrainian army, they refer me to her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.320
The life she depicts on social&nbsp;
media is not for the faint of heart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.320
She tells me, she used to be a fisher, then&nbsp;
served as a representative for her ethnic group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.040
the Sami people. She tells me that after&nbsp;
that, she trained as a combat medic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.840
Now, she says, she’s on the frontlines.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.120
First of all, it's a moral obligation.&nbsp;
This is home base. It's in Europe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.560
So if you can help, you should.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.760
She tells me what her days are like.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.040
You can't really prepare because you&nbsp;
don't know what's going to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.120
There might be an airstrike and it might&nbsp;
be artillery and it might be relocating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.600
So you just have to run by it day by day.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.720
On her social media account,&nbsp;
she poses with weapons.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.880
She tells me she has no&nbsp;
qualms about firing her gun.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.840
Well, it is what it is. It's your&nbsp;
job. It's what you have to do. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.600
it's the one who fires first. That's&nbsp;
how it goes. We are not the attackers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.440
We are the defenders. We are not the&nbsp;
one crossing any borders, they did.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.480
Kapon flies to Krakow in Poland,&nbsp;
close to the Ukrainian border.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.360
Temperatures in eastern Europe just have&nbsp;
dipped to near freezing - a climate that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.240
Kapon has never experienced before. I&nbsp;
join him for the next leg of his journey

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.560
First stop: A military shop.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.240
He still needs a bullet-proof vest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.240
since he isn’t sure whether the&nbsp;
international legion provides one.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:06:00.080
Do you have body armor? No? But&nbsp;
another body armor you have?

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:02.880
No

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.840
Five point eleven?

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.000
No, no, no, we don’t have.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.040
The military shops in Krakow&nbsp;
are overrun right now.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:12.880
What are you going to do?

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.160
Well, apparently, it’s difficult&nbsp;
to find body armor in Krakow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.760
I have to go without one, and&nbsp;
hope that I don’t get shot at.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.800
Isn’t that a suicide mission?

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:31.680
A bit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.280
It would be good to have one. But even&nbsp;
with a vest, the bullets come through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.880
So the only thing I can do is&nbsp;
hope to come back in one piece.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.840
By chance, Kapon meets some British&nbsp;
men who also want to join the battle.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.560
We go today.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.240
Ah, today, ok.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:54.320
Medic?

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.720
Yes, Paramedic.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.840
To me, he makes a dubious impression.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.080
Killer.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:11.440
Killer. Killer. Killer.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.920
The man doesn’t want to be filmed – but&nbsp;
claims he fought in Iraq and Afghanistan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:18.080
working for a private military contractor.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:29.840
Kapon has no combat experience, so he decides&nbsp;
to train on a shooting range. He is now joined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:36.480
by a man from Colombia who goes by Tato. They met&nbsp;
online in a group of Spanish-speaking volunteers.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.600
They also test an AK 47, which&nbsp;
is being used in Ukraine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.760
The training at the shooting range is intended&nbsp;
for civilians and is supposed to be just for fun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.840
It’s just the second time that Kapon&nbsp;
has ever held a gun, he tells me

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.880
After half an hour he’s done.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.640
It doesn’t prepare me for war as such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.800
but at least I know a how to handle a weapon&nbsp;
correctly, that I might use in Ukraine.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:21.040
For people like Kapon, the international&nbsp;
legion is their main port of call in Ukraine.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:26.480
On Instagram it advertises itself as an&nbsp;
adventurous, heroic group of comrades.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.680
It was founded just days after the war started&nbsp;
and is believed to have around 20 000 members.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:44.480
According to the legion, they are paid the&nbsp;
equivalent of Ukrainian soldiers of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:50.320
rank – sometimes less than 500 Euros a month.&nbsp;
Their contract lasts until the war is over.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.920
Their spokesperson tells me, that people who want&nbsp;
to join have to pass several tests in Ukraine.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:04.000
As a rule, they are sent to some of&nbsp;
the hottest spots on the front line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:12.000
and are taken care of in some very, let's say,&nbsp;
delicate, offensive and defensive operations.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:15.120
Can you prove that you don't&nbsp;
use them as cannon fodder?

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:22.320
Well, I think it is difficult for anyone to prove&nbsp;
anything in this war. What I can say is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:26.240
we can give all public and private assurances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:32.720
that no one in the Army is interested in&nbsp;
sending people to the front who are not ready.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.840
The Russian government sees the&nbsp;
international fighters as mercenaries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.320
which would violate international law and could&nbsp;
result in worse treatment if they are captured.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.440
I ask an expert for his opinion.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:51.120
They are not mercenaries. It's not a&nbsp;
company. It's not a commercial entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.400
which is sending those fighters&nbsp;
there. There is quite a difference.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:05.840
And as long as they are integrated into the forces&nbsp;
of the host country, they are not mercenaries.

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:10.720
Is this phenomenon of international&nbsp;
fighters that we see right now in Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.440
is this something new or has this always been&nbsp;
present also during other kinds of conflicts?

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:24.720
No, it’s not new. We've seen this in Afghanistan,&nbsp;
in Iraq and other Middle Eastern countries.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:33.680
But to make the distinction clear, when&nbsp;
those Islamist fighters joined an insurgency,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:41.040
it's completely different from joining&nbsp;
the ranks of an existing country.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.320
In Poland I meet a German soldier&nbsp;
who tells me he has been in Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.440
for 2 weeks. He wants to go&nbsp;
back to Ukraine with his dog.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:01.360
Poland seems to be a jumping-off point for&nbsp;
foreign volunteers. In total I talk to 7 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:09.040
them on and offline. Much of what they say is hard&nbsp;
to verify. Some of the men don’t appear credible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:14.187
their mental or social condition appears&nbsp;
unstable. A man from Estonia, who claims he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.187 --> 00:11:27.920
is at the front suddenly ends our contact, which&nbsp;
worries me. I am not sure what happened to him.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.640
I join Kapon and Tato on their way to the border.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.880
The international legion officially only accepts&nbsp;
people with live combat experience – but they give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:44.160
it a try anyway. Tato at least served for 8 years&nbsp;
in the Colombian military, he says. Recently he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:49.680
was working in Spain, but lost his job. For&nbsp;
him, the war is also a career opportunity.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:59.040
Why is it worth taking this risk? I often&nbsp;
ask myself that and don’t have an answer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:05.440
I think it’s also the excitement, the&nbsp;
adrenaline. It’s a chance to prove myself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.560
I think about it constantly and feel nervous.&nbsp;
I’d be lying if I said I wasn’t afraid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:23.840
but with this fear comes adrenaline.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.040
Time for the last voice message:

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:37.840
I want you to know that I am ok. I love&nbsp;
you. I’ll send you a message when I can.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:54.960
After death, I think god will judge us, for&nbsp;
what we did in life, whether it was good or bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.680
I’m grateful to my family that&nbsp;
they introduced me to Catholicism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:10.080
My faith gives me hope and keeps me safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:16.480
I know that I am going there for a good reason.&nbsp;
And if I don’t see my family and my friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:33.840
and the people I love here on this earth&nbsp;
again, I hope I will meet them after death.

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:39.840
The man who sits next to them is from Ukraine.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.000
That’s your family?

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:44.640
Yes, that’s my family.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:50.800
They are still in Ukraine. He’s going to the&nbsp;
border to get his mother and bring her to safety.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:57.040
His brother and cousin are at the front, he tells&nbsp;
me. So what does he think of the foreign fighters?

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:03.200
It good, they do a good job&nbsp;
for the peace in the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:11.040
and for peace in Ukraine. We cannot stop&nbsp;
this war by ourselves. We need help.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:14.240
This is the way to the border.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.920
Most people are going the opposite direction:

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.240
More than 5 million Ukrainians&nbsp;
have left their country so far.

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:33.600
I’m really cold and a bit nervous. Now that I see&nbsp;
the people here, the volunteers, the soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:38.320
the families crossing the border I’m even&nbsp;
more motivated and excited than I was before.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:46.960
Does he really think he can&nbsp;
change the course of the war?

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:51.200
I’m not Rambo, nothing special.&nbsp;
But each grain of sand helps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:57.840
And if I just save the life of a few&nbsp;
fighters, I’ll have achieved change.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.240
They want to join the&nbsp;
international legion the next day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:13.280
My journey with them ends here,&nbsp;
but they promise to stay in touch.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:25.760
I head back to Germany. I’m still in contact with&nbsp;
several people on their way to the international&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:32.960
legion. Some of them turn around the last minute.&nbsp;
And I receive sad news: The man from Estonia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:37.680
who said he was at the front and then stopped&nbsp;
communicating with me is no longer alive:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:45.600
His brother tells me, he returned home, but&nbsp;
then killed himself. His brother tells me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:50.400
he suffered from mental illness. He seemed to be&nbsp;
mentally unstable. Shortly before his suicide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:53.840
he apparently watched video clips of the war.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:03.120
Sandra, who has been at the front for quite some&nbsp;
time, is still there and determined to stay.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:06.000
Sandra:

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:14.400
There’s been a lot of bombing, left right and&nbsp;
above, everywhere. You get used to that, too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:23.280
The human brain is wired to just get used to&nbsp;
whatever situation you have to get used to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:30.720
And I know that sounds weird, but you can&nbsp;
get used to anything, including bombing.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.880
Yeah. When do you think? Will you be back home?

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:40.080
I will be back when this war is over. When there's&nbsp;
no more need for me here, then I will go home.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:48.560
Kapon seems to have a bit of a rollercoaster&nbsp;
ride. The international legion at first rejects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:54.800
him and several others. But 10 days later he&nbsp;
tells me the legion suddenly did accept him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.880
He writes ‘I am happy’ and sends me a&nbsp;
picture of the body armour he was given.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:07.040
On Instagram, he posts you are the only one&nbsp;
who can make all of your dreams come true.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:15.200
Besides paramedic tasks, he now seems to be&nbsp;
receiving regular combat training in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:20.160
to defend himself. In a few days,&nbsp;
he could be sent to the front.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:27.120
We agree that for security reasons&nbsp;
this will be our last interview.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:32.320
They will train me for combat,&nbsp;
with real ammunition, everything.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.240
Have you thought about leaving?

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.080
You do think about it when you hear detonations,&nbsp;
when you’re close to exploding grenades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:50.240
when you hear sirens and are in the&nbsp;
cold for hours, wearing just a sweater.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:59.840
Also, I haven’t showered in a week, since&nbsp;
there’s no bathroom. So you do start to think.

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:08.160
Has your view of this war changed?

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:12.080
Yes. I realized it’s even worse&nbsp;
than what you see on the news.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:18.800
Everything is worse, because you’re&nbsp;
the main target. It’s quite ugly.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:41.840
It’s a strange feeling to say goodbye and I&nbsp;
hope he will make it back home in one piece.

